  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 206 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nSouthwesterly flow will remain through at least the first part of \nnext week offering at least low storm chances, which are highest at \nnight, as weak shortwave troughs move through this flow. As the \nridge amplifies late in the week, this may aid in pushing the storm \ntrack farther away from Iowa. Temperatures will range from the 80s \nover northern Iowa to the 90s over southern Iowa with dewpoints well \ninto the 60s to low 70s. Heat index values will be well into the 90s \nto around 103 degrees or so most afternoon hours during next week. \nExperimental HeatRisk will reach the major/level 3 out of max of 4 \nto extreme/level 4 of 4 over southern into portions of central Iowa. \nThese high HeatRisk values are being driven by the uncommon late \nseason heat in concert with warm nighttime lows in the 70s with\nacclimation perhaps an offsetting factor.",
